        <body>
            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="0830" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg696"/>

                <head>No. 506.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Phelps.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-02-03"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 3,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 780.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith, for the files of your
                    legation, copies of the telegraphic correspondence which has taken place to
                    date, relative to fishing vessels in Halifax, about which I telegraphed to you
                    on the 31st ultimo.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F.
                        Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>






